    <string name="keyword_description">Listens for the words above in the audio Echo is already recording and sounds an alarm when one of them is heard, within a couple of seconds. Recognition happens on the phone, with no second microphone stream and nothing sent anywhere, and keeps working with the screen off. Several words can be given, separated by commas. Quiet stretches are skipped without being recognised, so this costs little over recording alone in a silent room, and rather more where there is talking to listen through.</string>
